      "h": "Reconstruct the lettered terrain",
      "c": [
        "c9-16-core"
      ],
      "html": "<h3>Rock units: identify the oldest foundation</h3><ul><li>G is granite basement. C lies above it and contains granite clasts, so G existed before C.</li><li>The lower sedimentary sequence is C then B then A. The higher sequence includes S and then K. Letters are names, not alphabetical age order.</li></ul><h3>Features: trace the physical contacts</h3><ul><li>F cuts older rocks; D crosses F, so the fault preceded the dike.</li><li>Old channels R interrupt the dike; canyon N truncates an old channel. Those relations place R after D and N after R.</li><li>Lava L poured into the already formed canyon and has little weathering or soil. It is younger than the canyon and youngest among the units requested in the source exercise.</li><li>Feature sequence: F→D→R→N→L. Granite G is oldest among the specified rock units; fault F is oldest among the specified later features. These are different comparison sets.</li></ul><h3>Add the isotope evidence</h3><ul><li>The table dates G at 1500 million years and D at 40 million years under the exercise assumptions.</li><li>Relative order does not supply an exact numerical date for every remaining event.</li></ul><p><a class=\"btn pri\" href=\"#exam2/cases/e2-c9a-terrain-investigation\">Start the terrain investigation</a> <button class=\"btn\" data-e2-practice=\"E2T17\">Practice geologic history</button></p>",
